    "code": "def solution():\n    # Define the monthly returns\n    tech_returns = [5.2, 3.8, 4.9, 2.7, 6.5, 3.3]\n    market_returns = [4.1, 3.9, 5.0, 2.5, 6.0, 3.7]\n\n    # Calculate the Pearson correlation coefficient\n    n = len(tech_returns)\n    sum_x = sum(tech_returns)\n    sum_y = sum(market_returns)\n    sum_xy = sum(x * y for x, y in zip(tech_returns, market_returns))\n    sum_x_squared = sum(x ** 2 for x in tech_returns)\n    sum_y_squared = sum(y ** 2 for y in market_returns)\n\n    numerator = n * sum_xy - sum_x * sum_y\n    denominator = (\n        (n * sum_x_squared - sum_x ** 2)\n        * (n * sum_y_squared - sum_y ** 2)\n    ) ** 0.5\n    correlation = numerator / denominator\n\n    # Return the coefficient rounded to four decimal places\n    return round(correlation, 4)\n"
